  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Rural song-dance of the Guantánamo region of eastern Cuba, played at country parties and regarded as a direct forerunner of son. Its ensemble is the tres, the bongó de monte (a larger, lower-pitched bongó that improvises throughout), the marímbula as bass, the guayo metal scraper and maracas, with a lead singer answered by a chorus. The bongos card stands in for the bongó de monte.",
